Doc 3(Title: "Alfonsina Storni") Alfonsina Storni Alfonsina Storni (29 May 1892 – 25 October 1938) was an Argentine poet of the modernist period. Storni was born into a middle-class family on May 29, 1892 in Sala Capriasca, Switzerland. Her parents were Alfonso Storni and Paula Matrignomi di Storni, who were of Italian-Swiss descent. Before her birth, her father had started a brewery in the city of San Juan, Argentina, producing beer and soda. In 1891, following the advice of a doctor, he returned with his wife to Switzerland, where Alfonsina was born the following year; she lived there until she was four years old.

